<# SAVE THIS FILE AS Export-InstanceMetadata.ps1

.SYNOPSIS
Exports SQL Server instance metadata for one or more instances into consolidated CSV inventory files.

.DESCRIPTION
Export-InstanceMetadata.ps1 connects to one or more SQL Server instances and
collects instance-level metadata using SQL Server Management Objects (SMO).

The script creates four output files:
- <FileBaseName>_Info.csv
- <FileBaseName>_Settings.csv
- <FileBaseName>_Config.csv
- <FileBaseName>_README.txt

These files are designed to provide an inventory view across multiple SQL Server
instances, rather than generating separate files for each server.

Metadata categories exported:

1. Information
   Server.Information properties such as version, edition, collation,
   operating system details, and related server attributes.

2. Settings
   Server.Settings properties exposed through SMO.

3. Configuration
   Server.Configuration properties similar to sp_configure values.
   Two rows are exported per instance in the configuration CSV:
   - ConfigValue
   - RunValue

.PARAMETER ServerInstance
One or more SQL Server instance names.

Examples:
- ProdSql01
- SQLServer1\SQL2019
- SQLNodeA\INST1,SQLNodeB\INST2

.PARAMETER OutputFolder
The folder where CSV files will be written.
If not specified, the current working directory is used.

.PARAMETER FileBaseName
Base file name used for the consolidated CSV files.

Default:
SQLInstanceMetadata

Example output files when FileBaseName is set to ProdInventory:
- ProdInventory_Info.csv
- ProdInventory_Settings.csv
- ProdInventory_Config.csv
- ProdInventory_README.txt

.PARAMETER SqlCredential
Optional SQL Server credential for SQL authentication.
If omitted, Windows authentication is used.

.EXAMPLE
.\Export-InstanceMetadata.ps1 -ServerInstance "ProdSql01"

Exports metadata for a single SQL Server instance using Windows authentication.
Creates these files in the current folder:
- SQLInstanceMetadata_Info.csv
- SQLInstanceMetadata_Settings.csv
- SQLInstanceMetadata_Config.csv
- SQLInstanceMetadata_README.txt

.EXAMPLE
.\Export-InstanceMetadata.ps1 -ServerInstance "SQL01","SQL02\INST1","SQL03" -OutputFolder "C:\SQL\Metadata" -Verbose

Exports metadata for multiple SQL Server instances and writes the consolidated
inventory CSV files to C:\SQL\Metadata.

.EXAMPLE
.\Export-InstanceMetadata.ps1 -ServerInstance "SQL01","SQL02" -OutputFolder "C:\SQL\Inventory" -FileBaseName "ProdSQLInventory"

Creates these files:
- ProdSQLInventory_Info.csv
- ProdSQLInventory_Settings.csv
- ProdSQLInventory_Config.csv
- ProdSQLInventory_README.txt

.EXAMPLE
$cred = Get-Credential
.\Export-InstanceMetadata.ps1 -ServerInstance "ProdSql01","ProdSql02" -OutputFolder "C:\SQL\Metadata" -SqlCredential $cred

Uses SQL authentication instead of Windows authentication and exports
consolidated inventory files for both SQL Server instances.

.EXAMPLE
.\Export-InstanceMetadata.ps1 -ServerInstance "SQL01","SQL02" -OutputFolder "C:\SQL\Metadata" -FileBaseName "Baseline" -WhatIf

Shows what the script would do without creating any files.

.EXAMPLE
"SQL01","SQL02\INST1","SQL03" | .\Export-InstanceMetadata.ps1 -OutputFolder "C:\SQL\Metadata" -FileBaseName "EstateInventory"

Passes SQL Server instance names through the pipeline and creates consolidated inventory CSV files.

.NOTES
Blog        : https://sqlpal.blogspot.com
Repository  : https://github.com/drupalgrupal/PowerShell/blob/main/SQL-Instance-Metadata-Export
Version     : 1.0.0
Created     : 2026-05-28
Updated     : 2026-05-28

Requirements:
- PowerShell 5.1 or later, or PowerShell 7.x
- SqlServer PowerShell module
- Network connectivity to target SQL Server instances
- Appropriate SQL Server permissions to view instance metadata

Install the required module:
Install-Module SqlServer -Scope CurrentUser

Help:
Get-Help .\Export-InstanceMetadata.ps1
Get-Help .\Export-InstanceMetadata.ps1
Get-Help .\Export-InstanceMetadata.ps1 -Examples
Get-Help .\Export-InstanceMetadata.ps1 -Detailed
Get-Help .\Export-InstanceMetadata.ps1 -Full

